messages:
Irene - DevEx: Heads-up: small bug in the Node sampleapp where x-request-id and traceparent get dropped on auth retry. Otel auto-instrumentation is enabled.

Cal - SDK: Likely because the retry helper rebuilds the fetch options and doesn't copy headers. Can you paste the retry snippet?

Moe - SampleApps: Minimal repro snippet: ```js
async function retryFetch(req) {
  const opts = { method: req.method, body: req.body }; // no headers
  const res = await fetch(req.url, opts);
  if (res.status === 401) { await refresh(); return retryFetch(req); }
  return res;
}
```

Irene - DevEx: Logs: "INFO incoming headers {x-request-id: r1}\nWARN auth refresh\nINFO outgoing headers {}" — so header exists initially then gone.

Priyanka - Infra: Two possibilities: header actually lost OR masked by redact rules. Check tenant redaction regex; avoid greedy patterns like ".*id.*".

Cal - SDK: Agreed. Short-term fix: copy headers into opts (headers: req.headers) or use Request.clone(). Medium-term: SDK http instrumentation should WARN once if context has an active span but outgoing request lacks propagation headers. I'll file a ticket.

Moe - SampleApps: Fixed in PR https://rwd.in/pr/6021 — change to `const opts = { ...req, headers: req.headers }` + added small unit test asserting x-request-id persists.

Irene - DevEx: Added docs blurb under onboarding: "When writing retry logic, preserve headers and propagation; avoid greedy redact regexes." Verified staging after PR, propagation stable. Closing. :white_check_mark:
